%% An abstract type is below itself alone, and not below the wildcard: "As the
%% endpoint of a simple prefix it matches only itself (Definition Prefix
%% Acceptance), and not the wildcard" (TGLP parameterized-types.tex, Definition
%% "Abstract Type").  pass/1 hands A?, at X, to sink/1, which declares `_?`:
%% by its abstract instance the head/body pair of A is not well-typed with
%% subtyping, the dual of A's head type, X, not being below `_`, so pass/1 is
%% not parametrically well-typed (Definition "Parametrically Well-Typed").  No
%% call instantiates it, so the program is rejected.  The reason: an
%% instantiation may put a structured type where X was, and by Definition
%% "Subtyping" a structured type is not below `_`.  Until 2026-10-12 an
%% abstract type was below the wildcard and pass/1 was certified.
procedure sink(_?).
sink(_).
procedure(X) pass(X?).
pass(A) :- sink(A?).
